# Apache configuration for the map. Upload this beside index.html.
#
# Everything here is inside an <IfModule> guard, so if a module is missing the
# directives are skipped rather than throwing a 500 and taking the site down.
# There is nothing here that the map needs in order to work — it is entirely
# about how much is sent down the wire and how long a browser keeps it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- compression
#
# Two things Apache gets wrong by default for this site.
#
# SVG is not on its compressed list, and two thirds of this site's weight is
# SVG: 5.3 MB raw against 1.5 MB gzipped.
#
# And `.js` is served as `text/javascript` by a current Apache and as
# `application/javascript` by an older one. A rule naming only one of them
# matches nothing on a server using the other, and then `map.js`, `data.js` and
# `cities-gaz.js` — 877 KB, which gzip takes to 261 KB — go down uncompressed
# with no sign that anything is wrong. Both spellings are listed.
<IfModule mod_deflate.c>
  AddOutputFilterByType DEFLATE text/html text/css text/plain
  AddOutputFilterByType DEFLATE text/javascript application/javascript application/x-javascript
  AddOutputFilterByType DEFLATE image/svg+xml application/json
</IfModule>

# and make sure the SVGs really are declared as SVG, or the rule above has
# nothing to match
<IfModule mod_mime.c>
  AddType image/svg+xml .svg
</IfModule>

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- caching
#
# The map's data changes only when it is rebuilt. `index.html` is small and
# carries the version number, so it is kept short: a reader who comes back gets
# the new page quickly and the heavy files from cache.
#
# If you are pushing changes during a teaching week, cut the seven days to an
# hour — otherwise somebody who visited on Monday sees Monday's map until the
# following Monday.
#
# The code is kept for an hour, not a week. `index.html` carries the version
# number and refreshes every ten minutes; if `map.js` were held for seven days
# a returning reader would get a fresh page reporting a fresh version over a
# week-old script, and the About dialog would say so with complete confidence.
# That happened: a bug that had been fixed and pushed was reported as still
# present, and the version number agreed with the reporter. An hour still saves
# almost all of the traffic — the geometry, which is two thirds of the weight
# and changes rarely, is what the seven days is for.
<IfModule mod_expires.c>
  ExpiresActive On
  ExpiresByType image/svg+xml          "access plus 7 days"
  ExpiresByType text/javascript        "access plus 1 hour"
  ExpiresByType application/javascript "access plus 1 hour"
  ExpiresByType text/css               "access plus 1 hour"
  ExpiresByType text/html              "access plus 10 minutes"
</IfModule>
